"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(n) complexity by time and O(n) by space.

The solution itself is elementary. 
But the logic behind deriving it is quite involved!
If I increase all elements except for one, they all go up while their relative differences remain the same
but the one that wasn't increased effectively decreases (relative to the others).
This allows us to reframe the problem as reducing all values ​​down to the minimum. 
Each move reduces the gap by one.
"""

class Solution:
    def minMoves(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:
        m = min(nums)
        return sum(elem - m for elem in nums)
